ZTE MF286R is a wireless LTE router, capable of connecting to LTE networks at download speeds up to 300Mbps using carrier aggegation. It has 3x3 2.4GHz Wi-Fi 4 and 2x2 5GHz Wi-Fi 5 Wave 2 radios, four gigabit ethernet ports, one USB 2.0 port, two RJ-11 ports for connecting landline phones that lets you use the cellular network to make calls. It is commonly used by some European ISPs for FWA(Fixed Wireless Access) services, such as Windtre on Italy, Turkcell on Türkiye, and more. Some models of the MF286 family include battery or phone ports, as well as corresponding LEDs on the front.

